{ build_physical_lrs.init - a DSEE derived object of be_com/lir.pas (lir.dir), included
  by lir.pas after solution_string_length.init (cc.a88k only),
  By build kind, the table of the physical registers' live ranges (25,
  26 lir_4090, 27, 28 lir_3f90): lir's data +0x0B8, 30 pointers.

  No Apollo copy survives; reconstructed from the DOMAIN C 6.9 binary
  cc.a88k, lir's .rwdi records (translator PA7).

  How the table is shared (docs/questions.md 161, translator PB2's
  scheme): lir.pas declares the variable `extern' and defines it, with
  the module's other cells, in address order (the image lays these
  tables out in the reverse of their include order: build_properties at
  +0 .. build_action at +0x3A0); this file gives it its initial value
  with a second `define' statement (the language reference's section
  7.2.2, method 2), which dpc accepts after the first and lays out where
  the first put the variable.

  Not known from the original: the element type. }

define build_physical_lrs := [
    nil, nil, nil, nil, nil, nil,  { 0 }
    nil, nil, nil, nil, nil, nil,  { 6 }
    nil, nil, nil, nil, nil, nil,  { 12 }
    nil, nil, nil, nil, nil, nil,  { 18 }
    nil, addr(lir_4090), addr(lir_4090), addr(lir_3f90), addr(lir_3f90), nil];  { 24 }
